and PERSISTS the backfill store relative to _confirm_peer_links (which opens its own fresh store via open_store and saves only when it wrote): state that backfill saves to disk before _confirm_peer_links opens, or that both share one store instance, so the described same-pass provenance upgrade actually holds.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile.py:537-543 — `_confirm_peer_links` calls `open_store(ctx.repo_root)` (fresh disk load) and `if written: store.save()`","Plan: backfill signature takes a `store` param but reconcile step says only 'invoke backfill ... immediately BEFORE the existing _confirm_peer_links call'","Plan claims a same-pass snapshot 'upgrades a backfilled record's provenance rather than being blocked by it' — which requires the backfilled records to be visible to _confirm_peer_links' fresh store instance"],"finding":"The same-pass provenance-upgrade mechanism depends on an unstated persistence/ordering detail: _confirm_peer_links opens its OWN store instance from disk and saves only when it wrote records, so backfill (given a separate store) must be persisted to disk BEFORE _confirm_peer_links opens its fresh instance for the described upgrade to occur.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0e5c57081aea890c","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope — reconcile.py::_persist_and_log bullet; AC8","norm_id":"ndfd5c2fb1830e377","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["Fresh upgrade pass where the current snapshot also observes one of the backfilled links: the snapshot record() overwrite only lands if the backfilled store was saved and re-read"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_stat